  "answer": "**Queensland** had the smallest decrease.\n\nThe rent-to-income ratio fell by only **1.75 percentage points** in Queensland (23.54% → 21.79%), compared to 1.87 pp in Victoria (22.90% → 21.03%) and 2.61 pp in NSW (25.57% → 22.96%).\n\n| State | 2016 Ratio | 2021 Ratio | Change |\n|-------|------------|------------|--------|\n| NSW   | 25.57% | 22.96% | **−2.61 pp** |\n| VIC   | 22.90% | 21.03% | **−1.87 pp** |\n| QLD   | 23.54% | 21.79% | **−1.75 pp** |\n\nAll figures from official ABS Census QuickStats for each state (2016 and 2021). Note: 2021 median rent excludes rent-free dwellings per ABS methodology; 2016 includes them.",
